<title>USA: Centennial group cuts Dreco Energy stake.</title>
<headline>Centennial group cuts Dreco Energy stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Centennial Energy Partners L.P. said Tuesday it cut its stake in Dreco Energy Services Ltd to 6.42 percent or 398,400 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the New York-based group said it sold a net of 93,300 shares of Dreco between November 14 and 22 at prices ranging from $30.00 to $38.50 a share.</p>
<p>Dreco is an Edmonton, Canada,-based oil and gas drilling equipment manufacturer, sales and rental company.</p>
